<p><strong>2. Narrowing the search space</strong><br>
<!-- -->Narrowing the search space involves progressively moving the left o=
r right pointer inward until the search space is reduced to one element or =
none.</p>
<p>At each point in the binary search, we need to decide how we narrow our =
search space. We can either:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Narrow the search space toward the left</strong> (by moving the=
 right pointer inward):</li>
</ul>
